From ccb5dad88e22c29da38f68cc5fb6de6995d38a12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:34:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/44] feat(chexc): capability lists cross package boundaries
 (proposal 3.10.2)

Closes ledger C1-C3. Until now a 'throws' clause stopped at the package edge:
imported declarations arrived capability-free, so cross-package checking was
silently absent rather than merely incomplete.

- C1: FuncTyInfo gains 'capTypes', written beside typeArgs (which holds the
  parameter types) and restored into GetFunctionTy on load. Keeping the list out
  of typeArgs mirrors the in-memory invariant: capabilities are erased for
  codegen and must never be mistaken for type arguments. Nested functional types
  ride along for free, so a clause inside a signature -- '(cb: () throws E -> R)'
  -- crosses too.
- C2: the incremental cache goes through the same SemaTy path, verified by an
  old/new test where the unchanged callee is served from cache and its
  requirement is still demanded at the call site.
- C3: NormalizeCapTys puts the exported list in canonical form -- entries
  subsumed by another dropped, remainder ordered by type name. Sound because a
  demand is per entry and discharged by subtyping: with 'A <: B' present, any
  supply discharging B discharges A, so {A,B} and {B} impose the same
  obligation. Reordering a clause is therefore no longer an ABI change; two
  orderings now produce byte-identical .cjo.

Also carries the 'captures' clause (3.9) across the boundary, which C1-C3 do not
cover but the guarantee needs: constructing an imported capturing class must
demand its captures. Imported declarations are rebuilt from the .cjo without
clause nodes, so ClassInfo/StructInfo store the list and the loader rebuilds the
clause from it.

Both schema fields are appended last, so a .cjo written before this change still
loads -- the vectors read as empty, which is exactly the pre-feature meaning.

One fix outside serialization: GetInstantiatedAccessorCapTys read the AST clause
only, so an imported PROPERTY ACCESSOR lost its list. It now falls back to the
functional type when the accessor is IMPORTED -- gated on that attribute, since
for source declarations the FuncTy also holds inference results, which must not
be re-read as declared entries.

Tests: compiler/CheckedExceptions/serialization, 10 cases across every boundary
shape (function, method, property accessor, generic both directions, functional
type, captures, canonical form, incremental). LLT Parser+Sema+CheckedExceptions
+IncrementalCompilation 5949/5954 (the 5 are the red-by-design conversions and
adapt groups); ctest 49/49.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
